 ## Build
 
 The selected kernel recipe builds `build/armcpu/libArmCpu.a` through `component:ArmCpu`. Enable its kernel configuration and verify the GIC/timer/PSCI resources using the platform adaptation procedure.
+
+## Edge scheduler initialization
+
+With ArmCpu revision `93a5030c5d983d0ef90f0fca93879d6e36ad1ba8`, `armcpu-edge=1` allows the last secondary CPU to call
+`ml_cpu_init_completed()`. Verify the selected XNU cluster matrix before enabling it. Keep the scheduler's matrix assertions:
+QoS restrictions must satisfy its monotonicity rules, which the cluster search uses for early exits.
+
+CPU discovery alone does not establish working cluster migration, idle accounting or power management. Check all three on
+the device. A governor must exclude absent/offline processors from load estimates and rebase accounting after they return.
+Record boost duration, display-driven frequency floors, L3 votes and missing idle or thermal controls in the device's porting record.
