+## Persistent Data publication
+
+Open and validate persistent backing before publishing the block device to APFS. The first container probe must read the
+same backing as later volume I/O. Attaching the overlay only after discovering the volume UUID can leave APFS holding
+seed checkpoints while reads already return persisted blocks.
+
+RamBlock revision `4be2d7eb05ef5a98126c91e0302c149140c0e3e1` attaches backing during volume selection. Aston stages a patch
+before both storage recipes to attach it before `registerService()`. Its source-storage startup already starts UFS first.
+A requested writable backend that cannot open must not publish a seed-only disk. Preserve the original installation seed
+and reset only through the explicit installation action. Check the source pin and build overrides before reusing this change.
+
+Verify capacity through APFS after mounting Data, then test local Files operations and persistence across a reboot.
+Host publication and overlay fixtures cannot establish filesystem health or application compatibility.
